## 2. RED-PROOF B — Break Wave 1 invariant (SPEC §2.3 A computeLineHash)

Condition asserted: `computeLineHash` is the deterministic 4-hex FNV-1a hash
of the trimmed line (`0000`–`ffff`); distinct lines hash distinctly; anchors
fail closed beyond the ±25-line window.

Sabotage (minimal):
  file: src/editors/hashline-tools.ts
  old: export function computeLineHash(line: string): string {\n  const text = line.trim();
  new: export function computeLineHash(line: string): string {\n  void line;\n  return "0000";
  Effect: every line hashes to the constant "0000" — collisions everywhere,
  drift-window test can no longer distinguish anchors.

$ bun test > /tmp/opencode/sabotageB.log 2>&1
